🚀 Feature
It would be great to be able to pass optional parameters to the forward method, for example:
class Attention(jit.ScriptModule):
    @jit.script_method
    def forward(self, attender, attendee, seq_length=None, mask=None):
        if mask is not None:
            ...
        if seq_length is not None:
            ...
        ...

Motivation
For operations such as self-attention, it is common to pass optional arguments, such as mask which enforces an autoregressive structure of the model. A lot of existing code already uses this approach, so this feature will make switching to JIT an easier task.
Pitch
Arguments to the script methods can take a default value of None. Any use of the underlying tensor can occur only inside the enclosing if ... is not None expression. I suppose it is possible to implement a separate compiled function for each combination of provided arguments, with specific implementation being chosen depending on which variant is being called.

